Positive control confirming the instrument was live at this dump: "Login"
tile + "Guest User" header (both present, both auth-gated to render ONLY
when isLoggedIn == false) alongside the STILL-present "Back" affordance.
Negative (asserted absent): "My Address" and "Logout" tiles — both present
one dump earlier under the same account, both gone here. AC4 (guest tiles
auth-gated) reconfirmed by the same transcript.

Mechanism identified by reading the diff: ProfileScreen's body is wrapped in
GetBuilder<ProfileController> (profile_screen.dart:50). MenuController.logout()
calls Get.find<ProfileController>().clearUserInfo(), which update()s that
controller and forces ProfileScreen to rebuild IN PLACE (no navigation event
needed). Since `isLoggedIn` is recomputed from AuthHelper.isLoggedIn() at the
top of build(), the SAME pushed route re-renders itself as the guest variant
automatically. Get.back() in the dialog's onYesPressed pops the DIALOG
overlay route (pushed by Get.dialog()), not the ProfileScreen page route
underneath it — so the reviewer's feared "Get.back() strands the user on an
authenticated-shaped screen" does not occur: the screen the user is left on
is the correctly-recomposed guest one.

Tapped "Back" next: landed cleanly on Home showing "Select Your Location"
(no stale address/personalized data — confirms Home is genuinely guest-shaped
too, not left in a stale authenticated state).

