Verdict for this check: PASS. The post-logout state is genuinely
signed-out and coherent (Guest User / Login prompt on the pushed
ProfileScreen, then a clean guest Home on Back) — not stranded, not an
infinite spinner, not stale authenticated UI. It reaches the doc's required
OUTCOME by a different, GetBuilder-reactivity-based MECHANISM than the
Get.offAllNamed the solution doc anticipated, not by that mechanism itself.
No breaks_ac; no task_bug filed for this item. Noted as a low-severity
follow-up only: the UX leaves the user ON the guest Profile screen rather
than returning them to Home/landing, which is a minor navigation-polish
question (does a just-logged-out user expect to land back on the page they
were on, guest-shaped, vs. bounced to Home?) — not a defect, not blocking.
